structure of T5\u00d73 pung + B7-B8-B9 chow + F2 pair. T2 and T3 are isolated and hard to develop.\n\nReason: My hand contains a strong T5 pung (3 tiles) and a potential B7-B8-B9 chow sequence with F2 as a pair. Discarding B3 eliminates an isolated tile that doesn't contribute to my most viable winning pattern. This keeps my T5 pung intact and maintains the B7-B8 sequence waiting for B9 (4 remaining), while preserving the F2 pair. This structure gives me the clearest path to a valid winning hand worth at least 8 points.\n\nAnswer: Play B3"}
