ential. Only 1 T8 remains unshown, and both T6 (1 left) and T9 (1 left) have very limited availability, making it nearly impossible to form a chow. Discarding T8 maintains my F2 pair (for potential Prevalent Wind pung), keeps T5 flexibility, and preserves T2-T3 which still has slight potential with the 1 remaining T1.\n\nAnswer: Play T8"}
